{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1508572-alternate-daeva-weakness-2nd-edition","id":1508572,"title":"Alternate Daeva Weakness (2nd edition)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-16T15:23:16-07:00","id":1508572,"title":"Alternate Daeva Weakness (2nd edition)","content":"Here's something I've been thinking about lately about the Daeva clan curse in 2nd edition.<br /> <br /> So each clans bane in 2nd has evolved into something similar to what they had in 1st, except for the daeva in my opinion<br /> Gangrel = animalistic mind (read idiot) &gt; animalistic urges (hard time controlling themselves)<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Are close to their beast with their intelligence &gt; with their urges (frenzy)</div> <br /> <br /> Nosferatu = ugly &gt; have a hard time interacting with humans (read ugly)<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Should avoid human interactions or risk breaching the masquerade</div> <br /> <br /> Mekhet = worse fire and sun bane &gt; worse bane effect and a custom bane<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Weaker vampiric nature</div> <br /> <br /> Ventrue = get insane as humanity goes lower &gt; harder to keep humanity due to touchstone (so get insane over time)<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Need to protect their humanity</div> <br /> <br /> Daeva = indulge your vice &gt; fall in love permanently with prey due to repeating feeding.\u200b<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">1st edition-Indulge your vice when you have the opportunity<br /> 2nd edition-Drinking anyone without care is dangerous<br /> My alternate bane-Indulge yourself in an addiction regularly</div> <br /> <br /> While each clan curses changes, I think the various banes mostly keep the mentality of the clan except for the daevas. In 1st, Daeves had to go fully in their consumption of everything, forced to act upon their vice most of the time. A bit forced to not think about the consequences if they want to keep their willpower high. But in 2nd, they have to be careful. Make sure that they have access to huge feeding grounds and herd to avoid feeding from someone twice in the prey life time (a bit bonkers that forever part). Since, as far as I know, a vinculum 2 mostly won't allow the vampire to kill the human or go extremely wild with it. The daeva will change its desire momentarily and seek to love and protect someone. But I agree its going to be in the f*ed up way vampires do. So here's my alternate clan bane<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><b>The Addictive Curse</b>\u200b<br /> Daeva always feel the need to indulge themselves into something. Like junkies, they hitch and feel weird when they can't get their fix. Daeva are permanently addicted to a set of action. It can be nearly anything as long as it is somewhat negative like being degrading, impulsive, a waste of time, and so on like gambling, spending countless time on social medias, being part of a fight club, etc. The Daeva must indulge in his addiction at least once every Humanity nights. Failure to do so gives the Daeva the Deprived condition until he gets his fix. Resolving the deprived condition and getting his fix never award beats and of course the addiction can never be resolved. The vampire may change his addiction whenever he gains or loses Humanity. The addiction cannot be linked to any of the vampire touchstones.<br /> <br /> <i>Example 1: A daeva like Marla from fight club goes to anonymous meetings and bangs whoever she can get afterward. This habit could be an healthy touchstone for a vampire, but as an addiction, now that's weird!</i><br /> <i>Example 2: This other Daeva is a real nerd and has always liked going to book clubs has a mortal. As an undead he still goes and while appearing as the most interesting person there would feel great, he never uses majesty. Often skip reading part of the book just to be able to argue more about the topic of the night. And arguing isn't about being in the right or wrong.<br /> Example 3: Now this Daeva humanity is really low and she can barely remembers how it was to be human. She does remember that she liked to go fishing and so every other nights she goes in the swamp to catch barehanded a fish, a lizard or sometime a bigger prey like an alligator. After she catches something, she always make sure to display her catch by leaving it at the nearest dock so that the morning people can see how big her catches are. </i></span><br /> <br /> This alternate weakness keeps 1st edition need to indulge in mind. The daeva can indulge as much as he wants and never have to fear feeding too much. The downside is to have an activity that provides no real advantages to the daeva. Maybe even endanger his requiem by having a touchstone-like habits that the vampire will have to protect. And the penalty of not doing the action is much more mechanical in nature.\u200b<br /> <br /> And while making an alternate Daeva bane, might as well make a worse version for Elders.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><b>The Bloody Curse</b><br /> In Daeva elders, the Addictive Curse degenerate toward the only real meaningful thing for vampires; blood. The elder is addicted to all kind of blood. This addiction changes how the elder feels his hunger, or rather that the elder is always hungry. Regardless of how much vitae the elder his holding inside of his body, he always feels the need to drink more even risking frenzy when he sees blood at any given time. This needs to drink blood is exacerbated by the fact that any blood, even those that cannot sustain nourishment to the vampire is still a risk of frenzy. This bane comes in three part. First, the vampire only feels not hungry when he is full of vitae. A single vitae spent means that the elder suffers a -2 penalty to resist frenzy. Secondly, the risk of frenzy to feed applies to all source of blood be it diluted blood in blood bags, animal blood, humans, vampire and other supernatural creatures that have a blood equivalent. Lastly, while the vampire may feel the urge to drink all sorts of blood, normal blood only provide nourishment by spending a willpower while drinking and blood from supernatural creatures requires the Unnatural Affinity merit as usual. If either condition aren't met, the vampire still drink the blood and its get stored in his body, but will provide no benefits when expanded.<br /> <br /> <i>Example 1: An elder daeva is walking in an hospital for whatever goal he has. Then suddenly, he makes a turn and sees the blood bank. You guessed it, the elder gorges himself in useless blood from blood bags making a mess for nothing.<br /> Example 2: The hitching and the thirst never fully go away. This daeva knows when he's full of blood. Heck he even made sure to protect his requiem by having a farm of revenants in his basement. But the thirst never fully goes away. Their blood always feels great and it's always so easy to drink more than necessary. Just to keep the taste in his mouth for a few more minutes. He even carries a bottle on himself to sate his thrist. But now, that throat dryness is starting again and he's so far from home with an empty bottle. Maybe just this once he'll drink some other vampire blood.</i></span><br /> <br /> Note: For the bloody curse, the player should note which vitae he has in his body that provides normal effect and which does not. A vampire won't awake from his daily torpor if the only blood in his body comes from non-nourishing source. The only benefit that blood from non-nourishing source provides is to remove the hungry penalty when the vampire is full of vitae.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3638,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3638-daganisoraan","user":"Daganisoraan","date":". 04-16-2023, 06:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3638-daganisoraan","name":"Daganisoraan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T15:49:06-07:00","id":1508577,"title":"","content":"Putting aside the really uncritical reductive read of the changes, the understanding of the bane in only one of two ways (at a minimum), and the personal preference of the Serpents Bane in Second Edition in general:<br /> <br /> 1) It'd be easier to just say Daevas retain a Vice anchor and otherwise impose the Addictive Curse as is.<br /> <br /> 2) THe Bloody Curse is both unncessarily punishing and doesn't really do a lot for being a narratively interesting wrinkle to operations. If you're going to rebuild the curses on the grounds of the Daeva's relationship to vice, and you're keeping it to an understanding of addiction as deep and abiding as their thirst for blood, then the next reasonable step is to either increase the effects of either the addiction or the withdrawal, or otherwise lean into the Daeva's role of tempters and make it clear that personal vice is no longer enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T23:46:32-07:00","id":1508609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1508572-alternate-daeva-weakness-2nd-edition?p=1508577#post1508577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Putting aside the really uncritical reductive read of the changes, the understanding of the bane in only one of two ways (at a minimum)</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you elaborate on this? What do you mean the understanding of the bane in only one of two ways?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3638-daganisoraan","name":"Daganisoraan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T00:05:35-07:00","id":1508610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daganisoraan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1508572-alternate-daeva-weakness-2nd-edition?p=1508609#post1508609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could you elaborate on this? What do you mean the understanding of the bane in only one of two ways?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a Vampire person, but Arcane probably means the reflection of Daeva being a bad relationship. You either spread the feeding around, hoping to not catch feels, or hyper focus on a single person or two. It\u2019s actually quite clever, it emphasizes the bad relationship personified nature of vamps, especially the ones themed around everyone loving them even when they shouldn\u2019t.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T00:57:02-07:00","id":1508618,"title":"","content":"Yeah, 2e Daeva are encouraged to build herds as much as they are to avoid feeding on the same mortal twice. Any immortal demigod of blood and sex isn't really fulfilling the archetype without a cult to lavish with affection and receive the praises of. Or for a more modern image stringing a dozen potential partners along without committing to any of them.<br /> <br /> Or being that drug dealer who just want stop pushing you to buy their product. I think I've got a new villain for a Hunter chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T15:26:23-07:00","id":1508673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1508572-alternate-daeva-weakness-2nd-edition?p=1508618#post1508618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, 2e Daeva are encouraged to build herds as much as they are to avoid feeding on the same mortal twice. Any immortal demigod of blood and sex isn't really fulfilling the archetype without a cult to lavish with affection and receive the praises of. Or for a more modern image stringing a dozen potential partners along without committing to any of them.<br /> <br /> Or being that drug dealer who just want stop pushing you to buy their product. I think I've got a new villain for a Hunter chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds doubly resonant for Daeva on account of <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Anvari\" target=\"_blank\">this bunch</a>.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T15:36:02-07:00","id":1508674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daganisoraan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1508572-alternate-daeva-weakness-2nd-edition?p=1508609#post1508609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could you elaborate on this? What do you mean the understanding of the bane in only one of two ways?</div> </div> </div> </div>For the most part, I won't, because I appreciate a homebrew effort that actually states it's goals and reasoning and then actually sets out to do that and I don't want to distract from it too much. Just-like, read things a little more critically. As others have pointed out, the Serpent's Bane in Second Edition has a number of consequences, and how you can handle it can take a couple of different forms depending on how you lean into or away from it.<br /> <br /> Anyways, back on track, One thing to make the earlier suggestion more balanced (Because three anchor points creates an excess of Willpower) that also can do with some questioning for how you want the Daeva to operate is to have Vice replace a character's Mask or Dirge. You can even have it be a player choice, but it depends on what you want out of your Daeva.<br /> <br /> The Daeva with Mask and Vice is perhaps the most balanced of the bunch, but probably leans more into the Daeva as liars and deceivers more than out and out hedonists, and as that might relate to the Elder version of the curse probably encourages a take that encourages tempting others into vice more than their own personal indulgence. Remembrance of humanity by filling an imitative role in Mask is not the same as being your best self affirmation in Virtue, and likewise, vampires may relate to the Daeva's connection and affection through Mask but are more alienated by how much less &quot;it's just my nature&quot; their Vice is in comparison to other's Dirge.<br /> <br /> The Daeva with Dirge and Vice are definitely more the hedonist, finding themselves both how they are monsters as a broad self-actualization and in their pettier and more self-destructive impulses, but it puts them in a position of absolutely flirting with villification-they neither try to hold onto their humanity through pretense nor feel rewarded personally by doing some kind of good. The Elder Curse version of this should probably double down on the indulgence. Then again, you might need to refigure out what the Daeva's saving grace is under this pretense and why they get indulged at Elysium's and build from there.<br /> <br /> The Daeva that leaves that to the player's choice is probably the variant with the least trust in the Daeva, because they just aren't consistent-but at the same time, the various extremis of the clan makes it easier to fit them into a wide variety of roles. No one will quite know what they get with a Daeva, only that where it goes will probably be a good time they'll end up regretting.<br /> <br /> Something to chew on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}